-- The module whose CONSTRUCTOR `entry.mdk` names with a `(..)` suffix.  `Jjw` is a
-- constructor of `QTW`, not a type, which is the whole point: the `(..)` has nothing
-- to expand.
--
-- `Kkw` is a SECOND constructor of the SAME type, present so that an over-expanding
-- `Jjw(..)` member has something wrong to drag in — see entry.mdk.
public export data QTW = Jjw Int | Kkw

export unQW : QTW -> Int
unQW (Jjw n) = n
unQW Kkw = 0
